.TH AI-EDITOR-CONFIG 1 "@VERSION@" "ai-editor-docker" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ai-editor-config \- configure the AI Editor service settings on the host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ai-editor-config
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIKEY=VALUE\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ai-editor-config
is the argument surface for \fB/etc/default/ai-editor\fR, the settings file of the
\fBai-editor-docker\fR package. Every value is validated before anything is written;
a rejected argument leaves the settings file untouched. After a successful write the
tool re-applies the result: it runs the config preflight and recreates the container,
so the change reaches the running service.
.PP
The settings are substituted into \fB/etc/ai-editor/ai_editor_container.json\fR as
\fB${AI_EDITOR_*}\fR placeholders when the container loads its configuration.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List every supported setting with its option, current value, and description.
.TP
.B show
Print the settings file.
.TP
.B get \fIKEY\fR
Print the value of one setting.
.TP
.B set \fIoptions\fR
Validate and write settings, then re-apply them. Use \fB\-\-no\-apply\fR to write
without recreating the container. Requires root.
.TP
.B init
Fill any setting the file does not carry yet with the package default. Never
overwrites a value that is already set. Run by the package on install. Requires root.
.TP
.B apply
Re-run the config preflight and recreate the container. Use \fB\-\-check\-only\fR to
run the preflight alone. Requires root.
.SH SETTINGS
.TP
.B \-\-port\fR, \fB\-\-bind\-host\fR, \fB\-\-advertised\-host\fR, \fB\-\-protocol
Published host port, in-container bind address, advertised host, and the
server/client/transport protocol (\fBhttp\fR, \fBhttps\fR, \fBmtls\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-registration\-host\fR, \fB\-\-registration\-port\fR, \fB\-\-registration\-protocol
MCP proxy endpoint used for register, unregister, and heartbeat.
.TP
.B \-\-code\-analysis\-host\fR, \fB\-\-code\-analysis\-port\fR, \fB\-\-code\-analysis\-protocol
Code Analysis server endpoint. The protocol accepts \fBhttp\fR or \fBhttps\fR only.
.TP
.B \-\-server\-id\-suffix
Suffix appended to \fBregistration.server_id\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-mtls\-dir\fR, \fB\-\-mtls\-container\-dir
Host directory holding the mTLS material, and its mount point in the container.
.TP
.B \-\-server\-cert\fR, \fB\-\-server\-key\fR, \fB\-\-server\-ca
Server certificate, private key, and CA bundle, as paths inside the container.
.TP
.B \-\-client\-cert\fR, \fB\-\-client\-key\fR, \fB\-\-client\-ca
Client certificate, private key, and CA bundle, as paths inside the container.
.TP
.B \-\-network\-primary\fR, \fB\-\-network\-secondary\fR, \fB\-\-dns\-name
Docker networks the container joins, and the network alias it publishes itself under.
A missing network is created on install and on recreate.
.TP
.B \-\-container\fR, \fB\-\-user\fR, \fB\-\-group
Container name and the system user and group owning the service files.
.SH DOCKER DNS
Container\-to\-container addressing goes by Docker network name, never by IP:
\fBcasmgr\fR for the Code Analysis server, \fBmcp\-proxy\fR for the proxy, and this
service publishes itself as \fBai\-editor\-server\fR. \fB\-\-dns\-name\fR rejects an
IP literal for that reason; a peer host accepts one but leaves Docker DNS behind.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
An argument was rejected. Nothing was written.
.TP
.B 3
Permission denied; run under \fBsudo\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ai\-editor\-config list
ai\-editor\-config get AI_EDITOR_REGISTRATION_HOST
sudo ai\-editor\-config set \-\-registration\-host mcp\-proxy \-\-registration\-port 3004
sudo ai\-editor\-config set AI_EDITOR_CODE_ANALYSIS_PORT=15010 \-\-no\-apply
sudo ai\-editor\-config apply
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/default/ai-editor
Settings file (dpkg conffile).
.TP
.B /etc/ai-editor/ai_editor_container.json
Service configuration template with \fB${AI_EDITOR_*}\fR placeholders.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ai-editor-docker (1),
.BR ai-editor-info (1)
